Deliberately unmodified from upstream
-------------------------------------
The rebrand renamed "Hermes" to "Eternal" throughout, with these exceptions,
which refer to things that are not the agent and would break if renamed:

  * LICENSE and the contributors/ records — legal and attribution integrity.
  * Hermes 3 / Hermes 4 model identifiers (e.g. "nousresearch/hermes-4-405b")
    and the regex that matches them — these are large language model names used
    for provider routing and for the non-agentic-model warning.
  * The "hermes-0day" indicator of compromise in eternal_cli/mcp_security.py —
    an attacker SSH key and campaign name in a security blocklist. Renaming it
    would silently disable that detection.
  * Upstream URLs (hermes-agent.nousresearch.com, github.com/NousResearch/
    hermes-agent, the nousresearch/hermes-agent Docker image) — these point at
    real upstream resources and must resolve.
